{
  "description": "Synthetic learners for the coach suite: three groups of five, one of each archetype in every group, so one group's run reads every kind of learner once. Each profile is the learner's work as the app records it -- the marks of every attempt in order (out of the part's maximum in PART_SPECS), the tagged errors with the learner's own words as evidence, the marked Writing bands -- and the suite seeds it into an in-memory database, so the snapshot the coach writes about is computed by the app's own SQL. 'reference' is one good review of that learner: it states their figures without opinion, says what is rising or slipping (or that there is too little data) and names what comes first. The paid judge (evals/judge.py) marks each report against it; nothing else scores the report. 'expect' keeps the reference honest: 'figures' are the numbers it states and 'targets' its first priority, both checked against the reference by metrics.answer_correct; 'priority' lists every acceptable first priority (a part, an error category or a Writing subscale), 'trend' the parts whose direction it states and 'insufficient' whether there is too little data for any trend -- all checked against the snapshot computed from the profile by tests/test_evals_offline.py.",
